From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:51:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dw_dp: Add system sleep PM ops

The PM core takes a runtime PM reference on every device in
device_prepare(), so the autosuspend that the bridge's atomic_disable
queues during drm_mode_config_helper_suspend() never runs and the DP
controller stays runtime-active across system suspend. Its power domain
(PD_VO0 on RK3588) is still switched off by genpd in the noirq phase,
because that only depends on the system-wide state of the devices in
the domain.

On resume the domain is powered on again, but the controller is still
marked runtime-active, so dw_dp_runtime_resume() is not called and the
registers set up by dw_dp_init_hw() (and the HPD software override in
the VO GRF) are lost. The atomic_enable from
drm_mode_config_helper_resume() then fails AUX transfers:

  dw-dp fde50000.dp: timeout waiting for AUX reply
  dw-dp fde50000.dp: failed to enable link: -110

and the display stays dark until the next full disable/enable cycle.

Use pm_runtime_force_suspend()/pm_runtime_force_resume() as late
system sleep callbacks. They run after the DRM device has been
suspended and before it is resumed, so the controller is properly
runtime-suspended before its power domain goes down and is re-initialised
by the regular runtime resume path when the bridge is enabled again.

Found on Orange Pi 5 (RK3588S) with a USB-C DP alt-mode monitor: with
pm_test=platform and with real s2idle the link fails on every resume. Not
yet tested on hardware with the fix (the DP sink was moved to HDMI).

Fixes the runtime PM support added in:
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260806-synopsys-dw-dp-improvements-v11-15-0d508505f383@collabora.com

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_dp-rockchip.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_dp-rockchip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_dp-rockchip.c
index 770ab042a187..59c66b657031 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_dp-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_dp-rockchip.c
@@ -271,6 +271,7 @@ static int dw_dp_rockchip_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops dw_dp_pm_ops = {
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(dw_dp_rockchip_runtime_suspend, dw_dp_rockchip_runtime_resume, NULL)
+	LATE_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 };
 
 static const struct rockchip_dw_dp_plat_data rk3588_dp_plat_data = {
